# ============================================================================
# Nuxel S10+ kernel config — Samsung Galaxy S10+ (beyond2lte, Exynos 9820)
# ============================================================================
#
# CORRECTION (2026-10-11): the S10+ kernel is NOT `linux-postmarketos-exynos9820`
# (that repo/package does not exist) and is NOT a mainline tree with a Kconfig
# fragment. The real, proven kernel is the DOWNSTREAM Samsung Exynos 9820 fork:
#
#   https://github.com/Linux4/android_kernel_samsung_exynos9820
#   commit f7194c1d15eded1c2a1a4dc63825b26103435cc0   (Linux 4.14.253)
#   in-tree defconfig: arch/arm64/configs/exynos9820-beyond2lte_defconfig
#
# The downstream tree brings its own complete defconfig (it already enables
# exynos DRM/DSI, sec_ts touch, bcmdhd WiFi, madera/SLSI audio, S3NRN82 NFC,
# FIMC-IS camera, UFS, etc.). Do NOT merge a fragment on top of it.
#
# Therefore this file is INTENTIONALLY INFORMATIONAL — the build wrapper
# (kernel/s10plus/build-kernel.sh) uses the in-tree
# exynos9820-beyond2lte_defconfig directly, not a merge.
#
# To actually build the kernel, run:
#   NUXEL_DEVICE=s10plus bash kernel/s10plus/build-kernel.sh --clone
#
# (For reference, a build on a native aarch64 Linux host with a modern GCC
# needs CROSS_COMPILE= and -Wno-error downgrades for the GCC 14/15 diagnostics
# that the 4.14 tree predates — the wrapper already applies these.)
